<user-part actor-type="user" name="Rob" user-id="oIAIJz43eqWLDyUxW7CMOYnj0Md2"></user-part>In the reference material you'll find the spec for our new game. I now want to talk through what the design of it will be. I want to zero in on the gameboard / gameplay since we can derive everything from that.

I want SUPER CLEAN. Almost like a blueprint. But I want the game pieces (whatever they may be. We haven't necessarily locked on ships. Especially given the hexagonal pattern. It might be a little odd. But I can imagine you having a shape on top of the lit up hexagons). It can be "rendered realistic" shapes (i.e. it can be stylized simplistic forms. It just needs to be super clean.) the intent is to have a blueprint like base on which realistic looking things sit on top. So think about an old World War II map with the actual physical things put on top.

Very similar to this:

